-<p>Energy is a supply question in Southcentral and the Interior, not only a price. ENSTAR, the gas utility, has said it could fall short of gas this winter, and in October 2026 the state favored ENSTAR's proposal in a contest between two plans to store gas in the Kenai Loop field [^30]. In the Interior, Golden Valley Electric Association issued its first-ever energy emergency alert in October 2026 [^31]. A study for a cold-storage, processing, data or lodging project with a large load asks the utility for a written service commitment and prices backup fuel, and it does not take an energy cost from a statewide average.</p>
-<p>Insurance after the 2025 storms began with the regulator. Alaska's Division of Insurance issued Bulletin B25-07 after the October 2025 storms with guidance to insurers, including a premium grace period for affected policyholders, as PropertyCasualty360 reported on October 16, 2025 [^32]. Rate filings and earthquake coverage take-up with a recent date were not found, so a study carries a quoted premium for the subject rather than a market rate.</p>
-<p>No construction cost index for Anchorage, Fairbanks or any other Alaska market was found from Rider Levett Bucknall, Cumming or Turner, and no wage determination was read. A budget is therefore supported by a contractor's bid or an independent cost estimate, with freight and the building season stated as their own lines, since materials reach many Alaska sites by air, by barge or over a long road haul.</p>
